# Filmklubben — AI Coding Rules

## Project
Swedish movie club website. Next.js 14 App Router, Supabase, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, Embla Carousel. Hosted on Netlify.

## Language
All user-facing strings in **Swedish**.

## Code Rules
- TypeScript strict — no `any`
- Named exports only (except Next.js pages/layouts which use default export)
- Files: `kebab-case`. Components: `PascalCase`
- Internal imports use `@/` alias
- API routes: validate with Zod, return `{ error: string }` on failure
- No comments unless WHY is non-obvious

## Auth
Single admin account. JWT stored in localStorage. Protected routes check `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. See `src/lib/auth.ts`.

## Database
Supabase PostgreSQL. Client in `src/lib/supabase.ts`. Two tables: `movies`, `ratings`. View: `movies_with_ratings`.

## Movie Extraction
`src/lib/tmdb.ts` for IMDb/TMDB URLs. `src/lib/ai-extract.ts` (Claude Haiku) for other URLs.

## Ratings
Session UUID in localStorage (`filmklubben_session`). 1–10 scale. Upsert on `(movie_id, session_id)`.

## Env Vars Required
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH, JWT_SECRET, TMDB_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
